# PRISM HW-MIGRATION FREEZE — ACTIVE MARKER
#
# The EXISTENCE of this file asserts the operator's hardware/drive-migration
# freeze is currently ACTIVE. While present, fleet-task-health-watch.mjs treats
# DELIBERATELY-DISABLED non-load-bearing PRISM scheduled tasks as an EXPECTED
# pause (informational) instead of a degraded safety net — so the every-Stop
# "scheduled-task safety net WARN" stops crying wolf on a state the operator
# intentionally created. (~47 tasks are frozen; the disabled set fluctuates
# across readings, so a marker — not a static list — is the only robust track.)
#
# SOURCE OF TRUTH (the human note this machine-readable marker mirrors):
#   .claude/helpers/install-vault-rot-sentinel-cron.ps1 lines 11-16
#   "DO NOT run this installer ... until the operator confirms the migration is complete."
#   Project memory: project_scheduled_task_migration_freeze_2026_06_08
#
# LOAD-BEARING TASKS ARE NEVER EXCUSED BY THIS MARKER: a disabled MUST_EXIST or
# crash-critical task (e.g. a reaper) still escalates — the operator would not
# freeze a load-bearing safety net, so a disabled one is a real signal.
#
# WHEN THE MIGRATION COMPLETES: DELETE this file. The watch will immediately
# resume flagging any still-disabled task as a degradation — your re-enable
# reminder surfaces exactly when it should. (Override without deleting:
# env PRISM_MIGRATION_FREEZE_ACTIVE=0 forces inactive even if this file exists.)
